-- seed.sql: local/dev sample data for Whoosh. Runs after migrations on `supabase db reset`.
--
-- WARNING: LOCAL/DEV ONLY. This file inserts fake users into auth.users.
-- It must NEVER be applied to the real (remote) Supabase project. `supabase db push` does not
-- run it; do not paste it into the remote SQL editor either.
--
-- Sample rides and near misses along Massachusetts Avenue, Cambridge and Boston (Harvard Square
-- to Boston Medical Center). Points are hand-placed approximations, not surveyed. The same data
-- is in web/fixtures/rides.json and web/fixtures/incident_cells.json; keep the three in sync.
--
-- Contents: three fake riders, 7 rides (3 shared, one per rider; 4 private), 17 near misses.
-- The 15 shared near misses form 5 incident areas that pass the public_incident_cells thresholds
-- (at least 3 reports from at least 2 riders, older than 24 hours): Central Square, 77 Mass Ave
-- at MIT, Beacon Street by the Harvard Bridge, Boylston Street, and Columbus Avenue.
-- Each area's points are kept inside one 0.001-degree cell (no point on a rounding boundary).
--
-- Conventions (see .kiro/team/supabase-contract.md):
--   * SI units. Timestamps are UTC. Routes are GeoJSON LineStrings in [longitude, latitude] order,
--     already privacy-trimmed; distance_m is the full ride (trimmed line plus 2 x 160 m).
--   * active_duration_s is 30 s less than the start-to-end span (time stopped at lights).

